Research Pack 1: Business AI Governance Foundation for Fede’s Item #5

Fede’s number 5 is asking for three connected governance designs:

1. Strategic use case scoping
    How business AI ideas get identified, submitted, assessed, prioritized, approved, piloted, measured, and scaled.
2. Cost and KPI measurement
    How BJ’s proves whether AI use cases are actually creating value, not just excitement.
3. Risk and appropriate-use governance
    How BJ’s enables AI use while protecting members, team members, business data, brand trust, and operational integrity.

The core research finding is this:

Modern AI governance is shifting away from static policy documents and toward operating systems: intake, risk tiering, KPI baselining, human review rules, tool/data access controls, pilot gates, and ongoing monitoring. NIST frames AI risk management around govern, map, measure, and manage; ISO/IEC 42001 frames AI governance as a management system with policies, objectives, processes, risk assessment, and continual improvement; OECD emphasizes trustworthy, human-centered AI that respects rights, fairness, privacy, and democratic values.  

