Will the use case affect employees or employment-related decisions?

Risk increases if AI influences:

* hiring;
* performance evaluation;
* scheduling;
* disciplinary decisions;
* promotion decisions;
* compensation;
* workforce reduction;
* employee monitoring;
* training assignment;
* HR case handling.

The EU AI Act is not necessarily the governing law for BJ’s US operations, but its risk categories are useful as a global benchmark: high-risk AI includes contexts such as employment, education, essential services, critical infrastructure, biometric uses, law enforcement, migration, and justice.  

7. Data involved

Identify whether the use case touches:

* public data;
* internal non-confidential data;
* confidential business data;
* member personal information;
* team member personal information;
* vendor/supplier confidential data;
* financial data;
* legal material;
